ShortDescription: @DESCRIPTION@
Description: |-
  llmman points coding agents such as Claude Code, Codex and OpenCode at a
  model running on your own machine, or at any hosted provider, in one
  command: `llmman launch claude --model qwen3.8` starts a local inference
  server, downloads a llama.cpp build matching your GPU, loads the model and
  execs the agent against it. Models are stored as standard OCI artifacts,
  so they pull from Docker Hub, Hugging Face or any OCI registry (GHCR,
  quay, Harbor, self-hosted) and transfer between registries in one step.
  `llmman serve` exposes an Ollama-, OpenAI- and Anthropic-compatible
  endpoint, and several daemons can pool their hardware into one.
